 d=\"M2 9a3 3 0 0 1 0 6v2a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-2a3 3 0 0 1 0-6V7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2Z\"></path><path d=\"M13 5v2\"></path><path d=\"M13 17v2\"></path><path d=\"M13 11v2\"></path></svg></div><div><h3 class=\"font-bold text-gray-900 text-lg leading-tight\">Free Entry</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5\">Official booking required</p></div></div></div><article class=\"prose prose-lg prose-headings:text-slate-900 prose-p:text-slate-700 prose-a:text-blue-600 prose-a:font-semibold prose-img:rounded-xl max-w-none\"><div class=\"mb-10 text-xl font-medium text-slate-800 leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6 py-1\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Ramadan is the holy month of fasting, introspection, and prayer for Muslims. In 2026, it is expected to begin on <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">February 17</strong> (subject to moon sighting). This guide covers everything from prayer timings to the best Iftar tents in the UAE.</p></div><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Ramadan 2026 in the UAE is expected to begin on <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Tuesday, February 17, 2026</strong>, subject to the official moon sighting announcement. As the holiest month in Islam, Ramadan is a time of fasting, prayer, reflection, generosity, and community.</p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">In the UAE, Ramadan is also a unique cultural experience, with special prayer timings, reduced working hours, late-night dining, and exclusive Iftar and Suhoor deals across Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, and other emirates.</p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">This guide covers <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Ramadan 2026 UAE dates, timetable, fasting hours, working hours, and practical planning information</strong> — all in one place.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">When Does Ramadan 2026 Start in the UAE?</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Astronomically, <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Ramadan 2026 is expected to start on February 17, 2026</strong>. However, the official start date will be confirmed by the <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">UAE Moon Sighting Committee</strong>, as Islamic months depend on the sighting of the crescent moon.</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Expected start:</strong> February 17, 2026</li><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Expected end:</strong> March 18 or March 19, 2026</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Ramadan 2026 UAE Start and End Dates (Expected)</h2><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg w-full\"><table class=\"w-full text-base text-left border-collapse\"><thead class=\"bg-gray-50\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-200\">Event</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-200\">Expected Date</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-gray-100 bg-white\"><tr class=\"bg-white\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Ramadan begins</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">February 17, 2026</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-gray-50/50\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Ramadan ends</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">March 18 or 19, 2026</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Eid al-Fitr</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">March 19 or 20, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">⚠️ Dates may vary by one day depending on moon sighting.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">How Many Days Is Ramadan 2026 in the UAE?</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Ramadan 2026 in the UAE is expected to last <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">29 or 30 days</strong>, depending on the sighting of the new moon. This variation is normal in the Islamic calendar and applies across all emirates.</p><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Ramadan 2026 UAE Timetable (Expected Prayer &amp; Iftar Times)</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Below is an <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">approximate Ramadan 2026 UAE timetable</strong>. Timings may vary slightly by emirate and date.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Ramadan 2026 UAE Timetable Table</h3><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg w-full\"><table class=\"w-full text-base text-left border-collapse\"><thead class=\"bg-gray-50\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-200\">Prayer</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-200\">Approximate Time</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-gray-100 bg-white\"><tr class=\"bg-white\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Fajr (Fast begins)</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">5:05 – 5:15 AM</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-gray-50/50\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Sunrise</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">6:25 – 6:35 AM</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Dhuhr</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">12:25 – 12:35 PM</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-gray-50/50\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Asr</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">3:40 – 3:55 PM</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Maghrib (Iftar)</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">6:20 – 6:35 PM</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-gray-50/50\"><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-gray-900 w-1/3\">Isha &amp; Taraweeh</td><td class=\"px-5 py-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed \">7:45 – 8:00 PM</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\"><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Note: </strong>Always follow local mosque announcements or official prayer calendars for daily accuracy.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Fasting Hours During Ramadan 2026 in the UAE</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Fasting during Ramadan lasts from <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Fajr (dawn)</strong> until <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Maghrib (sunset)</strong>.</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li><strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Average fasting duration:</strong> 13–14 hours</li><li>Fasting hours gradually increase as Ramadan progresses</li><li>Applies across Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, and other emirates</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Ramadan 2026 UAE Working Hours</h2><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Private Sector</h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">According to the UAE Labour Law, <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">private sector employees are entitled to a reduction of two working hours per day</strong> during Ramadan.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Public Sector</h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Public sector working hours are announced separately by the UAE government authorities closer to Ramadan.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Schools</h3><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Many schools operate on <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">reduced schedules</strong>, depending on the curriculum and emirate.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Best Iftar Experiences in the UAE During Ramadan 2026</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Iftar, the meal that breaks the fast at sunset, is one of the most anticipated moments of Ramadan in the UAE.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">Popular Iftar Options</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Luxury hotel Ramadan tents</li><li>International Iftar buffets</li><li>Traditional Arabic Iftar menus</li><li>Affordable Iftar deals at local restaurants</li></ul><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Common Iftar items include dates, soup, grilled meats, rice dishes, and traditional desserts like <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">kunafa and luqaimat</strong>.</p><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Suhoor in the UAE: Late-Night Ramadan Culture</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Suhoor is the pre-dawn meal eaten before Fajr. In the UAE, Suhoor often becomes a relaxed late-night social experience.</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Many cafés and Ramadan tents remain open until 2–3 AM</li><li>Popular Suhoor menus include light Arabic dishes, juices, and tea</li><li>Home-delivered Suhoor meal plans are widely available.</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Ramadan Shopping &amp; Special Deals in the UAE</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Ramadan is a major shopping season in the UAE.</p><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-800\">What to Expect</h3><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Discounts on groceries and essentials</li><li>Modest fashion and abaya collections</li><li>Ramadan gift hampers</li><li>Special offers on electronics and home items</li></ul><hr class=\"w-full my-6 border-t border-gray-200\"/><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Charity and Giving During Ramadan in the UAE</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Charity is central to Ramadan. Many residents participate in:</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Zakat and Sadaqah donations</li><li>Community Iftar distributions</li><li>Ramadan food box initiatives</li><li>Verified online charity campaigns</li></ul><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">How Ramadan 2026 Leads Into Eid al-Fitr</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Ramadan concludes with <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Eid al-Fitr</strong>, marked by:</p><ul class=\"list-disc ml-6 space-y-3 mb-8 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary text-lg\"><li>Eid prayers</li><li>Family gatherings</li><li>Festive meals</li><li>Public celebrations across the UAE</li></ul><h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-3\">Final Thoughts: Ramadan 2026 in the UAE</h2><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Ramadan 2026 in the UAE is a time of spirituality, discipline, generosity, and community. From structured fasting schedules and prayer timings to memorable Iftar gatherings and meaningful charity initiatives, the holy month offers a deeply enriching experience for residents and visitors alike.</p><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">🌙 <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">Ramadan Kareem from TopTenUAE.com</strong></p></article><div class=\"mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-gray-100\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 flex items-center gap-2\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class=\"bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-12\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50/50\"><h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 flex items-center gap-3\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-6 h-6 text-primary\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class=\"divide-y divide-gray-100\"><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">When does Ramadan 2026 start in UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Ramadan 2026 in the UAE is <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">astronomically expected to begin on Tuesday, February 17, 2026</strong>. The official date will be confirmed by the UAE Moon Sighting Committee.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">What are the working hours during Ramadan 2026 in the UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Private sector employees in the UAE typically receive a <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">two-hour reduction in daily working hours</strong> during Ramadan. Public sector timings are announced separately by the authorities.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">When is Eid al-Fitr 2026 in the UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Eid al-Fitr 2026 in the UAE is <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">expected to fall on March 19, 2026</strong>, subject to the official moon sighting.</p></div></details><details class=\"group [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 md:p-6 text-gray-900 font-bold group-open:bg-blue-50/30 group-open:text-blue-700 transition-colors select-none\"><h3 class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-snug\">How long are fasting hours during Ramadan 2026 in the UAE?</h3><div class=\"relative shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 md:w-8 md:h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-50 group-open:bg-blue-600 text-blue-600 group-open:text-white transition-all duration-300 mt-0.5\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-plus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-100 rotate-0 group-open:opacity-90 group-open:rotate-90 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"M12 5v14\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-minus absolute w-4 h-4 md:w-5 md:h-5 opacity-0 -rotate-90 group-open:opacity-100 group-open:rotate-0 transition-all duration-300\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path></svg></div></summary><div class=\"px-5 md:px-6 pb-6 pt-2 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-base\"><p class=\"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-gray-900 text-base\">Fasting hours during Ramadan 2026 are expected to range between <strong class=\"font-extrabold text-gray-800\">13 and 14 hours per day</strong>, from Fajr until Maghrib.</p></div></details></div></div></div></div></main><aside class=\"w-full lg:w-80 shrink-0 space-y-8 mt-12 lg:mt-0\"><div class=\"bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"absolute top-0 right-0 w-24 h-24 bg-primary/5 rounded-full translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2\"></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4 mb-4 relative z-10\"><div class=\"w-14 h-14 bg-gray-50 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden border-2 border-white shadow-md\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-shield-check w-7 h-7 text-[#4b0082]\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2